message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Network capacity is sometimes compute capacity: an accounting framework and decision boundaries for infrastructure investment in large-scale AI training"
abstract: >-
  An accounting framework that assigns every accelerator-second in a large
  synchronous training job to one of four mutually exclusive fates, a
  substitution metric that expresses an infrastructure improvement as the
  equivalent accelerator purchase, and decision-boundary maps identifying which
  marginal infrastructure investment yields the most productive accelerator time
  in each operating regime.
